{"t_ms": 9162, "stream": "stdout", "data": {"event": "result", "result": {"conversation_id": "84f9a66c-abf4-49f9-81bc-07fe9d6ef1a6", "status": "SUCCESS", "response": "Here is a quick guide to using **Antigravity (AGY)** and its available slash commands:\n\n### Available Slash Commands\n\n* **/plan** – Initiates detailed step-by-step planning and architecture design before making code changes.\n* **/grill-me** – Starts an interactive interview/review session to refine requirements and architectural decisions.\n* **/goal** – Sets a high-level, long-running goal where the agent works autonomously and thoroughly until completion.\n* **/schedule** – Sets up one-shot timers or recurring cron jobs for periodic checks and background tasks.\n* **/browser** – Directs browser automation, testing, and web research workflows.\n* **/learn** – Teaches the agent preferences, project rules, or recurring setup procedures to persist across future sessions.\n\n---\n\n### What I Can Help You With\n\n* **Code Exploration & Editing**: Search codebase, view/edit files, run tests, and debug issues.\n* **Refactoring & Feature Development**: Plan, implement, and verify multi-file features.\n* **Automation & Subagents**: Run concurrent tasks, terminal commands, or delegate complex tasks to subagents.\n* **Customizations**: Configure [skills](file://<HOME>/.gemini/antigravity-cli/builtin/skills/agy-customizations/SKILL.md), workspace rules, hooks, and MCP servers.\n\nLet me know what you would like to work on!\n", "duration_seconds": 8.84160525, "num_turns": 1, "usage": {"input_tokens": 37027, "output_tokens": 575, "thinking_tokens": 0, "cache_read_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 37602}}}}
